NAME
    qemu-run.sh - start a prepared m-boot raw disk image under QEMU

SYNOPSIS
    tests/qemu-run.sh --target x86_64-efi|arm64-efi|i386-pc --image FILE
                      [--firmware-code FILE --firmware-vars FILE] [--headless]

DESCRIPTION
    Launches QEMU with a new, temporary UEFI variable store for UEFI
    targets. The guest disk runs in QEMU snapshot mode: guest writes are
    not persisted to the original raw image. Interactive graphical output
    is used by default, because the embedded GRUB menu uses its console
    display and is NOT guaranteed to be visible on a serial-only terminal.

FIRMWARE
    x86_64-efi: qemu-system-x86_64 and a matching OVMF CODE/VARS pair.
    arm64-efi:  qemu-system-aarch64 and a matching AAVMF/edk2 CODE/VARS pair.
    i386-pc:    qemu-system-x86_64 and the QEMU BIOS (no external firmware).
    Common system locations are searched; pass both firmware paths if absent.
    No NVRAM template is altered by the test.

EXAMPLES
    tests/qemu-run.sh --target x86_64-efi \
      --image ./qemu-out/m-boot-x86_64-efi-loader.raw
    tests/qemu-run.sh --target arm64-efi \
      --image ./qemu-out/m-boot-arm64-efi-recovery.raw \
      --firmware-code /usr/share/AAVMF/AAVMF_CODE.fd \
      --firmware-vars /usr/share/AAVMF/AAVMF_VARS.fd

LIMITATIONS
    The command only launches QEMU; it does not judge boot success.
    --headless hides the graphical GRUB menu and is useful only for a
    configured serial/debugging workflow. Inspect the actual menu before
    reporting a working bootstrap or recovery.

